-#
  USR-08: what saving does stands before the fields, for a crew with the
  notices of its phones, which go with its sessions, and with the API key of
  a user who has one (BR-13). Inside the dialog a short key would be looked
  up among the words of the dialog itself, so the keys are written in full.
= render layout: "dialog", locals: { title: t(".title", name: @user.name) } do
  %p.caution
    = t(@user.crew? ? "user_passwords.edit.signs_out_crew" : "user_passwords.edit.signs_out", name: @user.name)
    = t(@user.api_key_issued_at ? "user_passwords.edit.former_and_key_stop" : "user_passwords.edit.former_stops")
  = form_with model: @user, scope: :user, url: user_password_path(@user), method: :patch, class: "form",
    data: { turbo_frame: "_top" } do |form|
    = render "passwords/field", form:, user: @user, field: :password, kind: "new-password"
    = render "passwords/field", form:, user: @user, field: :password_confirmation, kind: "new-password"
    .form-answers
      = form.submit t("user_passwords.edit.submit"), class: "button button-danger"
      %button.button.button-secondary{ type: "button", data: { action: "dialog#close" } }= t("common.cancel")
